{
  "_comment": "Every kind of enemy, and the cards each one fights with. A monster on the map is a group of one kind (a pack of zombies, a gang of raiders...); in battle the group is one enemy with `hp` health per member, so members fall as you wear it down. sprite: column of client/assets/sprites.png. speed: how long it takes to step on the map (x the server's step time: lower is faster). value: XP and scrap per member killed, as a share of a zombie's. size: [fewest, most] members (zombies use PACK_SIZE_WEIGHTS in server/src/monsters.ts); dungeons cap it. spawn: relative chance of appearing in the overworld and in dungeons, times 4 on a favoured tile. moves: its deck: each card goes in `weight` times, shuffled, and it shows the next one it'll play as its intent; `min` is the fewest members that can play it, `hurt` only when wounded, `noRepeat` never twice running. reactions: each group gets one (if it has `reactMin` members, `reactChance` of the time), used at most once a round when its `trigger` comes up, before what it answers lands. Numbers are fixed, or {base, per}: base + 1 per `per` members. Move effects: damage (x hits), all (hits you and every ally), block, weak, vulnerable, poison, discard (cards from your hand), strength, heal, summon (members). Reaction triggers: attacked, attacked_all (by a card or ally that hits every group), other_attacked, block_card, heal_card, reaction_card, ally_card. Reaction effects: block, strike (hits whoever it answers), poison (on whoever it answers), counter, strength, heal, summon.",
